<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cambodian–Vietnamese War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1978">1978</a>–<a href="/years/1989">1989</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Vietnamese invasion of Cambodia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cambodian–Vietnamese War was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a> regime of Democratic Kampuchea, which had launched border raids. Vietnam invaded in December 1978, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phnom-penh">Phnom Penh</a> in January 1979 and installed the People's Republic of Kampuchea. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> Rouge and other resistance groups fought on from the Thai border until Vietnamese troops withdrew in 1989.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cambodian-vietnamese-war.jpg" alt="Cambodian–Vietnamese War" width="320" height="289" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BorysMapping · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vietnamese_invasion_of_Cambodia.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
